WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:07.450
Buying a new car is for most citizens of Serbia an unattainable dream,

2
00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:12.050
and for those few who somehow manage to afford this pleasure,

3
00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:15.070
the purchase can turn into a real nightmare.

4
00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:19.350
Such a sad experience is shared by several buyers from Lazarevac and its surroundings,

5
00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:24.090
who wanted to buy a Fiat 500L through an official Fiat dealer,

6
00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:26.950
the company MSD Trade from Obrenovac.

7
00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:31.550
As Branko Simić and Aleksandar Stamenković told us,

8
00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:35.370
they chose the Fiat 500L partly because

9
00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:38.170
they considered it a reliable option,

10
00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:41.150
since the state also stands behind the Fiat project.

11
00:00:41.470 --> 00:00:46.530
Branko made the decision to buy back in spring 2013,

12
00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:49.670
and found the dealer through the official Fiat website.

13
00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:55.030
Through the internet I found out where there are showrooms at all

14
00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:57.870
where I could buy, pay for a 500L.

15
00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:02.930
I saw that in Lazarevac, which is closest to where I live — and that's where I went,

16
00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:08.590
there on May 20 I got an invoice for payment, and there we agreed.

17
00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:15.610
In mid-June the bank had already fulfilled its obligation to the dealer,

18
00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:18.790
and I had already made four payments to the bank.

19
00:01:19.870 --> 00:01:24.510
In the contract concluded between "Crédit Agricole" bank and Branko,

20
00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:29.690
it's clearly visible that it was signed on June 19, 2013,

21
00:01:29.870 --> 00:01:34.530
and according to our information, rarely does more than one working day pass

22
00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:37.850
before the bank transfers the money to the dealer or to Fiat.

23
00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:44.350
That is, the dealer received the money from the bank, probably as early as June 20, 2013,

24
00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:47.630
and then Branko's months-long wait began.

25
00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:51.010
As Branko told us, for the incredible delay,

26
00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:55.110
as MSD Trade claimed, everyone was to blame except themselves.

27
00:01:56.570 --> 00:02:00.650
They made excuses with Fiat, Fiat's vacations,

28
00:02:00.650 --> 00:02:02.670
the fact that Fiat doesn't supply the product.

29
00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:10.330
In November 2013, nearly five months after the bank transferred the money to the dealer,

30
00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:12.050
FAS informed us that

31
00:02:12.050 --> 00:02:16.170
FAS had not received any payment from MSD Trade

32
00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:19.370
in connection with the purchase of a car in the name of Branko Simić.

33
00:02:19.930 --> 00:02:23.030
After months of waiting it's no surprise

34
00:02:23.030 --> 00:02:27.030
that in November 2013 Branko told us that...

35
00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:31.530
Well, honestly, I lost all trust in him long ago,

36
00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:34.210
because a couple of times I talked with him by phone,

37
00:02:34.210 --> 00:02:40.730
and he constantly lied, let's say.

38
00:02:41.810 --> 00:02:44.670
He kept postponing the deadline: seven days, then another seven days,

39
00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:48.030
then next Monday, one thing and another — and then suddenly "bye."

40
00:02:48.910 --> 00:02:53.190
Branko is not the only buyer who didn't get the car by the agreed date.

41
00:02:53.410 --> 00:02:56.890
In the same situation was Aleksandar Stamenković,

42
00:02:56.890 --> 00:03:03.290
who, together with his father, wanted to buy a "people's Fiat" through MSD Trade.

43
00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:08.850
Aleksandar told us he was afraid of being left without both money and a car,

44
00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:12.110
because MSD Trade wasn't meeting delivery deadlines

45
00:03:12.110 --> 00:03:14.910
even for the cars that other buyers had paid for him.

46
00:03:15.770 --> 00:03:19.930
I was on the phone with at least three or four more people from Lazarevac,

47
00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:23.590
I think there are five of them in all — the ones who were cheated,

48
00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:27.610
cheated, in my opinion, literally: the cars still haven't been delivered.

49
00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:32.270
Through his connections Aleksandar managed not only to find out

50
00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:35.990
that his car had been standing for several months on the factory grounds,

51
00:03:35.990 --> 00:03:39.470
but, as he claims, also to get photos of his car

52
00:03:39.470 --> 00:03:42.250
waiting to be shipped at the factory parking lot.

53
00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:46.550
From the sticker it's clearly visible that the car is intended for MSD Trade

54
00:03:46.550 --> 00:03:52.010
and that it was produced on September 3, 2013 or even earlier.

55
00:03:52.430 --> 00:03:55.530
At first Aleksandar was angry only at the dealer,

56
00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:59.050
but over time he came to think that Fiat had let him down too.

57
00:03:59.770 --> 00:04:04.110
What disappointed me most was this: when I had to go to the bank,

58
00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:07.810
give money, take money — everyone checked me,

59
00:04:07.810 --> 00:04:10.630
while him, for example, this dealer, nobody checked.

60
00:04:11.030 --> 00:04:12.830
They only check whether we are creditworthy,

61
00:04:12.830 --> 00:04:15.530
but don't check whether the dealer is able to deliver the car.

62
00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:17.710
In this situation I'm angriest at Fiat most of all.

63
00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:22.190
Although it doesn't seem so now,

64
00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:27.170
FAS surely carried out at least some basic check of MSD Trade.

65
00:04:27.430 --> 00:04:33.750
According to available reports, MSD Trade has existed since 1992.

66
00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:37.250
For the past few years the company operated at a profit.

67
00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:40.830
The annual net profit of this enterprise from its core business

68
00:04:40.830 --> 00:04:45.210
in 2012 was almost 5 million dinars.

69
00:04:45.490 --> 00:04:51.370
However, in November 2013 MSD Trade's accounts were blocked

70
00:04:51.370 --> 00:04:55.590
due to debts of more than 24 million dinars.

71
00:04:55.770 --> 00:05:00.390
At MSD Trade they told us that the reason for the months-long delivery delay

72
00:05:00.390 --> 00:05:02.290
was that their accounts turned out to be blocked.

73
00:05:03.190 --> 00:05:05.670
It's hard to believe the explanation

74
00:05:05.670 --> 00:05:10.630
that Branko didn't receive the car because of the blocking of MSD Trade's accounts,

75
00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:16.170
since the bank transferred the money for Branko's car to MSD Trade back in June,

76
00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:22.150
and MSD Trade's accounts have been blocked only since October 31, 2013.

77
00:05:22.410 --> 00:05:28.270
That is, the block came two months after the car's delivery deadline had expired.

78
00:05:28.270 --> 00:05:33.630
Why MSD Trade didn't transfer the bank's payment for Branko's car to FAS

79
00:05:33.630 --> 00:05:34.950
remains unclear.

80
00:05:35.210 --> 00:05:39.610
After we first, in November 2013,

81
00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:43.290
aired a story about problems with the delivery of the Fiat 500L,

82
00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:48.290
the waiting of Aleksandar Stamenković and Branko Simić came to an end.

83
00:05:49.050 --> 00:05:51.450
Whether by chance or not, literally two days

84
00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:55.790
after your story aired I received the car.

85
00:05:56.810 --> 00:06:01.690
We're sure Branko and Aleksandar would have received their cars even without our story.

86
00:06:01.850 --> 00:06:04.770
At the moment when the first cars were delivered,

87
00:06:04.770 --> 00:06:08.930
MSD Trade informed the other buyers and us that

88
00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:15.210
the deadline for delivery of all cars was December 15, 2013.

89
00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:21.190
Delivery would proceed in the order in which payments arrived in MSD Trade's account.

90
00:06:21.990 --> 00:06:24.630
As the other buyers told us,

91
00:06:24.630 --> 00:06:28.470
MSD Trade acted in accordance with its public promise.

92
00:06:29.290 --> 00:06:33.310
We picked up our cars on December 16.

93
00:06:33.310 --> 00:06:39.570
So in this respect the dealer in a way met the deadline.

94
00:06:41.050 --> 00:06:46.170
Besides public apologies, FAS and MSD Trade did something concrete

95
00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:49.410
to somehow compensate buyers for the fact

96
00:06:49.410 --> 00:06:52.630
that they surely were nervous while waiting for delivery.

97
00:06:52.630 --> 00:06:57.470
From Fiat I received an extension of the warranty from two to four years,

98
00:06:57.470 --> 00:07:04.230
and from the dealer two free vouchers for the first two services,

99
00:07:04.230 --> 00:07:06.690
and I should note that too, in fairness.

100
00:07:07.130 --> 00:07:10.970
I was refunded the money for installing the air conditioner, 650 euros.

101
00:07:12.150 --> 00:07:15.710
Buyers told us they simply can't understand

102
00:07:15.710 --> 00:07:20.390
how FAS allowed an official Fiat dealer to, as they claim,

103
00:07:20.390 --> 00:07:23.070
take money paid in for Fiat cars

104
00:07:23.070 --> 00:07:26.090
and use it for other, personal purposes.

105
00:07:26.290 --> 00:07:28.950
They also told us why, in their opinion,

106
00:07:28.950 --> 00:07:32.450
there was a delay in delivering the paid-for cars.

107
00:07:32.450 --> 00:07:40.400
So that Mr. Vesić could invest all this money in his real estate.

108
00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:44.980
That is, in Obrenovac there are photos, there is documentation:

109
00:07:44.980 --> 00:07:51.340
on Tamnavska Street he's building a complex of buildings with our money.

110
00:07:51.340 --> 00:07:58.030
From buyers we also received photos of a building in Obrenovac,

111
00:07:58.030 --> 00:08:02.650
whose construction, as they suppose, was financed like this:

112
00:08:02.650 --> 00:08:06.770
the money MSD Trade received from buyers of Fiat cars

113
00:08:06.770 --> 00:08:10.050
was redirected to cover the construction costs of the building.

114
00:08:10.050 --> 00:08:12.590
At MSD Trade they told us that...

115
00:08:12.590 --> 00:08:16.210
The information you received from buyers is not true.

116
00:08:16.390 --> 00:08:22.170
MSD Trade is a business company with no connection to any construction in Obrenovac,

117
00:08:22.170 --> 00:08:27.110
it deals exclusively with providing all kinds of services related to the Fiat brand.

118
00:08:27.110 --> 00:08:34.150
Neither the owner nor the manager of MSD Trade participated in financing the building in Obrenovac,

119
00:08:34.150 --> 00:08:37.510
so the said question has no significance whatsoever

120
00:08:37.510 --> 00:08:41.770
for the specific problem that arose with buyers of the ordered cars.

121
00:08:41.770 --> 00:08:48.110
However, as buyers told us, MSD Trade and "Vesić Investgrad" —

122
00:08:48.110 --> 00:08:51.230
the company listed as the investor

123
00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:54.610
on the sign next to the building on Tamnavska Street in Obrenovac —

124
00:08:54.850 --> 00:08:58.990
are linked by the fact that during the period when car delivery was delayed,

125
00:08:58.990 --> 00:09:01.970
they had the same director — Dragan Vesić.

126
00:09:02.090 --> 00:09:06.050
Dragan Vesić confirmed to us that he was the director

127
00:09:06.050 --> 00:09:10.190
of the residential building under construction on Tamnavska Street and that...

128
00:09:14.190 --> 00:09:19.870
Dragan Vesić also claims that "Vesić Investgrad"

129
00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:23.170
has absolutely no connection with MSD Trade.

130
00:09:23.430 --> 00:09:25.790
We note that these two business companies

131
00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:30.090
are also in no way connected with each other as far as finances go.

132
00:09:30.310 --> 00:09:34.810
The information you received, as you yourself said, from buyers

133
00:09:34.810 --> 00:09:37.970
and which concerns the financing of the building, is not true.

134
00:09:39.250 --> 00:09:43.210
The fact that Dragan Vesić was director in both enterprises,

135
00:09:43.210 --> 00:09:46.290
although it indicates a link between the two companies,

136
00:09:46.490 --> 00:09:48.790
is at the same time not irrefutable proof

137
00:09:48.790 --> 00:09:52.370
that funds flowed from one company to the other.

138
00:09:52.610 --> 00:09:56.430
Whether construction was financed with the funds of car buyers —

139
00:09:56.430 --> 00:09:58.570
this should certainly interest the responsible persons at FAS,

140
00:09:58.710 --> 00:10:03.770
whom we also asked whether MSD Trade will remain an official Fiat dealer.

141
00:10:03.770 --> 00:10:06.350
As we were told at FAS...

142
00:10:16.020 --> 00:10:19.580
The problems faced by Fiat car buyers

143
00:10:19.580 --> 00:10:23.360
increasingly arise for buyers of other brands of cars too.

144
00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:26.640
Besides, the number of buyers is growing who,

145
00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:32.280
even with enforceable court rulings, are left without both a car and money,

146
00:10:32.440 --> 00:10:34.000
because the dealer went bankrupt,

147
00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:37.620
and it was registered as a limited liability company.

148
00:10:37.620 --> 00:10:42.480
Considering that new car sales are falling year after year,

149
00:10:42.480 --> 00:10:47.200
it's clear that many car sellers will have a very hard time staying afloat,

150
00:10:47.300 --> 00:10:49.720
and buyers, when buying a car,

151
00:10:49.720 --> 00:10:53.440
will have to analyze the dealer's financial stability too.

152
00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:56.900
A general idea of a dealer's current financial stability

153
00:10:56.900 --> 00:11:02.380
can be obtained by searching for enforced-collection debtors on the National Bank's website

154
00:11:02.380 --> 00:11:05.180
and studying the balance sheets on the APR (Business Registers Agency) website.

155
00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:10.080
And yet few people can adequately assess a seller's financial stability,

156
00:11:10.080 --> 00:11:13.960
and in Serbia it's hard to buy a car directly from the manufacturer,

157
00:11:14.020 --> 00:11:18.720
so in most cases we are exposed to various risks and whims of dealers.

158
00:11:18.880 --> 00:11:23.460
Since there is a possibility to buy a car directly from the manufacturer,

159
00:11:23.460 --> 00:11:27.800
as in the case of Fiat cars, it's worth taking advantage of that possibility.

160
00:11:27.800 --> 00:11:30.720
FAS has its own showroom in Belgrade,

161
00:11:30.720 --> 00:11:35.200
so if you're buying Fiat cars, that's the most reliable place to buy.

162
00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:40.660
True, Fiat salespeople most likely won't offer you free floor mats,

163
00:11:40.660 --> 00:11:44.140
an alarm or some other bonus, as other dealers do.

164
00:11:44.140 --> 00:11:49.680
But is it worth even thinking about extras that cost maybe a hundred euros,

165
00:11:49.680 --> 00:11:53.340
or a discount of a couple of hundred euros when buying a car

166
00:11:53.360 --> 00:11:55.680
that costs more than 11,000 euros,

167
00:11:55.680 --> 00:12:00.200
and is it worth risking, because of a relatively small sum,

168
00:12:00.200 --> 00:12:05.480
getting problems similar to those the buyers from Lazarevac had?